title: 西醫舉隅 / Xi yi ju yu [Gleanings of Western medicine]
version: 0.4.0
authors:
- family-names: Chu
  given-names: Chen-Yu
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9738-6914
url: https://github.com/poplolioi11/bodleian-sinica1842-xiyi-juyu-1875
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: Xi yi ju yu [Gleanings of Western medicine] compiles John Dudgeon’s medical articles from Zhong
  xi wen jian lu, catalogued as an 1875 [Peking] edition and held as Bodleian Sinica 1842. Its five prefaces
  and articles on the heart, circulation, eyes and forensic medicine support studies of late Qing medicine,
  translation, visual knowledge and publishing. This release preserves 25 title, preface and contents
  faces and supplies revised text for 28 complete prose faces and 13 selected diagram-label or table layers.
  JSON, TXT and TEI retain source characters, notes, uncertainties and links to the original; other existing
  periodical texts are linked rather than copied. AI independent readings were compared through nonblind
  source-image adjudication; full human collation has not been performed and unresolved readings are marked.
